  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Response to Humanitarian Needs of Afghan Returnees from Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of 4 November 2023, 261,200 Afghans returned from Pakistan through Torkham and Spin Boldak border points. It is estimated that 65 per cent of undocumented Afghan returnees from Pakistan are expected to require immediate post-arrival humanitarian assistance and protection. With winter approaching, winter related needs in a context of harsh climate conditions are increasing.Through this project, IOM is addressing the immediate post-arrival humanitarian needs of vulnerable undocumented and Afghan Citizenship Card (ACC) holder returnees from Pakistan with transportation assistance; shelter and household essential non-food items (NFIs) support; and camp coordination and camp management in the areas of return. The interventions also address immediate winterization needs (winter clothing, blankets, heating, fuel) of affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
